WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:03.648
Open Optional Integrations, N K P Framework.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:08.277
This is a preview workspace for the configured N K P ZeroTouch framework,

00:00:08.491 --> 00:00:11.886
profiles, binaries, schema and guarded phases.

00:00:12.123 --> 00:00:16.091
A ready profile or generated document is not a completed Kubernetes

00:00:16.177 --> 00:00:16.881
deployment.

00:00:17.158 --> 00:00:21.168
Review the exact installed integration, available commands and environment

00:00:21.211 --> 00:00:23.762
requirements before planning any target mutation.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:27.926
Use the profile and schema views to prepare the intended management or

00:00:27.969 --> 00:00:29.548
workload-cluster inputs.

00:00:29.804 --> 00:00:34.326
Review networking, registry, binaries and the selected framework revision.

00:00:34.753 --> 00:00:37.705
Keep saved profiles and credential references protected.

00:00:38.055 --> 00:00:42.065
A template is an operational starter, not a guarantee that its generated

00:00:42.236 --> 00:00:45.692
values satisfy every environment or current provider schema.

00:00:45.948 --> 00:00:49.071
Resolve unknown or blocked findings before proceeding.

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:53.654
Review the N K P readiness view and the binary or bundle inventory required

00:00:53.824 --> 00:00:55.019
by the chosen path.

00:00:55.403 --> 00:01:00.224
For an isolated site, verify actual artifacts, registry access and network

00:01:00.352 --> 00:01:01.218
dependencies.

00:01:01.529 --> 00:01:05.667
A checklist score can record preparation and evidence; it does not prove

00:01:05.795 --> 00:01:07.395
Kubernetes workloads are running.

00:01:07.715 --> 00:01:11.349
Confirm the real command versions and target-side results separately.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:15.757
Inspect the available phase, command preview and approval policy before

00:01:15.928 --> 00:01:16.611
submission.

00:01:16.995 --> 00:01:22.456
Schema, validation, parsing, generation, registry or plan-related actions

00:01:22.797 --> 00:01:23.893
have different scopes.

00:01:24.221 --> 00:01:28.146
A phase name alone does not establish that a full provisioning lifecycle is

00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:29.704
implemented and verified.

00:01:30.152 --> 00:01:33.394
Follow the returned blockers and supported installed behavior.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:37.141
Do not turn off safeguards to make an unavailable phase execute.

00:01:37.465 --> 00:01:41.689
Find N K P Validation Evidence under Advanced Automation with its Preview

00:01:41.903 --> 00:01:42.351
badge.

00:01:42.585 --> 00:01:47.236
Select the correct evidence source and profile, including the retained Z T F

00:01:47.364 --> 00:01:49.403
U A T packs where appropriate.

00:01:49.692 --> 00:01:54.172
Record the actual scope, review findings and export a sanitized pack.

00:01:54.556 --> 00:01:58.481
This workspace is not a general A H V cluster-health monitor and does not

00:01:58.524 --> 00:02:01.023
replace independent operational acceptance.
